# Guest init actions for the cpu-sec-bench NEMU platform (busybox init).
#
# Verbatim port of cpu-sec-test-env scripts/riscv64_nemu/venue/guest/inittab
# (2026-10-31).
#
# /proc and /sys are mounted first: the bench's own support library reads
# /proc/self/maps (lib/common/temp_file.cpp, get_region_base), so without
# /proc the stack-region ASLR case opens nothing, sees a zero base in both of
# its runs, and misreports "no ASLR" -- measured 2026-10-20: the guest scored
# 0 where the native host reference scores 1.  /dev needs no line here (the
# kernel mounts devtmpfs itself: CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y).
#
# sysinit actions run before the once action, so the bench always sees the
# mounted trees.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::once:/bench/bench.sh
